                                                            ONE TO MANY

🔹 Relationship between Entities?
       - It defines how multiple entities are related to each other.
       - At least 2 entities required.


Q1. One-to-Many kya hota hai?
        - Ek entity ka multiple records dusri entity se related hota hai.
        - Lekin dusri entity ka sirf ek record pehli entity se related hota hai.
👉 Simple Words:
        - One Applicant → Many Applications
        - Many Applications → One Applicant

 ✅ Real-Time Examples
          - Ek Applicant multiple Applications submit kar sakta hai.
          - Ek Customer multiple Orders kar sakta hai.
          - Ek Department me multiple Employees ho sakte hain.

                      +-------------------------+                     +----------------------+
                      |       Applicant         |                     |   Applicantions      |
                      +-------------------------+  1                * +----------------------+
                      | id          (PK)        |---------------------| id          (PK)     |
                      | name                    |                     | status               |
                      | email                   |                     | positions            |
                      | mobile                  |                     | applicant_id (FK)    |
                      | status                  |                     +----------------------+
                      +-------------------------+


🧭 One-to-Many Mapping ke Types :
          1️⃣ Unidirectional One-to-Many
              👉 Sirf Parent entity ko child ka reference pata hota hai.
              Example:  Applicant  --->  Applications
Applicant Entity (Parent) :
---------------------------
@Entity
public class Applicant {

    @Id
    @GeneratedValue(strategy = GenerationType.IDENTITY)
    private Long id;

    private String name;
    private String email;
    private String mobile;

    @OneToMany
    @JoinColumn(name = "applicant_id") // FK in Applications table
    private List<Application> applications;
}
Application Entity (Child) :
----------------------------
@Entity
public class Application {

    @Id
    @GeneratedValue(strategy = GenerationType.IDENTITY)
    private Long id;

    private String status;
    private String position;
}
👉 Yaha Application ko Applicant ka reference nahi pata.


      2️⃣ Bidirectional One-to-Many :
          👉 Dono entities ek dusre ko janti hain.
          Example: Applicant  <---->  Applications

Applicant Entity (Inverse Side) : Inverse Side = wo side jo relationship ko control (own) nahi karta.
--------------------------------
@Entity
public class Applicant {

    @Id
    @GeneratedValue(strategy = GenerationType.IDENTITY)
    private Long id;

    private String name;

    @OneToMany(mappedBy = "applicant")
    private List<Application> applications;
}
Application Entity (Owning Side) :
----------------------------------
@Entity
public class Application {

    @Id
    @GeneratedValue(strategy = GenerationType.IDENTITY)
    private Long id;

    private String status;
    private String position;

    @ManyToOne
    @JoinColumn(name = "applicant_id") // FK
    private Applicant applicant;
}

📌 Owning Side vs Inverse Side :
| Side         | Meaning                  |
| ------------ | ------------------------ |
| Owning Side  | Jis table me FK hota hai |
| Inverse Side | mappedBy wala side       |
👉 Foreign key always Owning Side me hota hai (Application table).


🔹 Important Annotations :
✅ @OneToMany
         Parent side mapping ke liye.
✅ @ManyToOne
         Child side mapping ke liye.
✅ @JoinColumn
         Foreign key column create karta hai.
✅ mappedBy
         Batata hai ki FK dusri table me hai.

🛑 Circular JSON Problem
Bidirectional mapping me infinite recursion hota hai:  Applicant → Application → Applicant → Application ...
Solution:
@JsonIgnore  : Jis side pe lagaya → wo JSON me show hi nahi hoga
or
@JsonManagedReference
@JsonBackReference

| Annotation              | Kis Side Pe Lagate Hai?    | Meaning           |
| ----------------------- | -------------------------- | ----------------- |
| `@JsonManagedReference` | **Parent Side (One side)** | JSON me show hoga |
| `@JsonBackReference`    | **Child Side (Many side)** | JSON me hide hoga |



